<!--{"title": "Case study: AI provider resilience under CPS 230", "description": "How an Australian insurer can treat AI model providers as material service providers under CPS 230: critical operations, tolerances, fallbacks and tested exit plans.", "short": "AI provider resilience under CPS 230", "h1": "When the model is a material service provider: AI resilience for an Australian insurer under CPS 230", "kicker": "Case study · Operational resilience", "lede": "An Australian general insurer had put AI into claims intake, customer service and fraud review, mostly through one hosted model provider. Nobody had asked what happens when that provider is slow, out of capacity or gone. Under APRA's CPS 230 that is a board-level question, and the goal was a credible answer.", "date": "2026-10-29", "datetime": "2026-10-29T13:05:00+04:00", "readtime": "9 min read", "sector": "Insurance · Australia", "role": "Fractional CTO and AI architect", "engagement": "Assessment, architecture and delivery leadership", "scope": "Critical operations mapping, AI service provider risk, multi-provider routing, degraded modes, exit testing", "stack": ["Model gateway", "Two hosted model providers", "Private model fallback", "Kubernetes inference routing", "Rules-based degraded mode", "OpenTelemetry", "Service provider register", "Scenario testing"], "outcomes": ["AI dependencies mapped to the critical operations they support", "Tolerance levels agreed for each AI-assisted operation", "Failover to a second provider or a rules-based mode, tested in production", "An exit plan for the primary model provider that has actually been rehearsed", "Board reporting that names AI providers alongside other material suppliers"], "tags": ["ai", "architecture", "governance"], "keywords": ["CPS 230", "APRA operational risk", "AI service provider risk", "material service provider AI", "AI resilience insurance", "model provider exit plan", "multi-model routing", "OAIC AI guidance", "fractional CTO Australia", "AI business continuity"], "faq": [["Does CPS 230 apply to AI model providers?", "CPS 230 covers operational risk, business continuity and the management of service providers for APRA-regulated entities. If an AI provider supports a critical operation, it belongs in that framework like any other material service provider; how your arrangements are classified is a question for your risk and legal teams."], ["What is a degraded mode for an AI-assisted process?", "A defined way to keep the operation running when the model is unavailable: a second provider, a smaller private model, or rules and human handling, with known limits on volume and quality."], ["How do you test an exit plan for a model provider?", "Run real traffic for an operation through the alternative path for a set period, measure quality, cost and latency against tolerance levels, and record what broke. A plan that has never carried traffic is not a plan."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-australia/", "/ai-architect/", "/technical-due-diligence/"], "citations": [{"title": "APRA provides an update on the implementation of new operational risk standard", "url": "https://www.apra.gov.au/news-and-publications/apra-provides-an-update-on-implementation-of-new-operational-risk-standard", "publisher": "APRA"}, {"title": "Operational risk management", "url": "https://www.apra.gov.au/consultations/operational-risk-management", "publisher": "APRA"}, {"title": "Guidance on privacy and the use of commercially available AI products", "url": "https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-guidance-for-organisations-and-government-agencies/guidance-on-privacy-and-the-use-of-commercially-available-ai-products", "publisher": "OAIC"}, {"title": "Microsoft's cloud growth accelerates, and so too does the spending", "url": "https://fortune.com/2026/10/28/microsofts-cloud-growth-accelerates-and-so-too-does-the-spending/", "publisher": "Fortune", "date": "28 Oct 2026"}, {"title": "Introducing Gateway API Inference Extension", "url": "http